# ============================================================
#  MAIN CHAIN: The Hollow Star
#
#  Something sleeps beneath the lake, sealed by Lumenhold's
#  founders. Kael Dumont's family serve it. Progress follows the
#  arc (content/world/arcs.grim): the clock advances on schedule,
#  beats leave leads, and the clues you followed them to are
#  counted by clues(hollowstar) (X11; the beats are in
#  chain_hollowstar_acts.grim, the clues in world/clues.grim).
#    leads          the archive or the Restricted Section, the boathouse,
#                   Maud, Kael, Seraphine, the seventh tower
#    clues >= 2     grey visitors
#    clues >= 3     the headmistress
#  Alignment (Lumen + / Hollow -) is the moral axis: the Star's
#  gifts pull toward the Hollow; refusing them, toward the Lumen.
#  Finale (final year, Blossomtide): hs_the_night -> hs_tunnel ->
#  hs_threshold -> hs_beneath (menu); the seal can fail (hollow_failed),
#  for those who engaged (or whom the Star has claimed, alignment <= -60).
#  Outcomes fill the yearbook's mystery line: sealed / bargained /
#  freed (alignment <= -60) / failed / claimed (game over) / bystander.
# ============================================================

@event hs_dreams_begin
time: morning
title: The Black Star Dream
class: story
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 5 and clock(hollowstar) >= 1 and not has(hollow_dreams)
weight: 14
art: moon
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A dreamscape: a frozen lake seen from beneath, a round door glowing at the bottom, and above it a star that is a hole in the sky.
text: You dream of the lake from underneath. There is a round door at the bottom, and above the water a star that is not a light but an absence. A voice says your name like it is tasting it. You wake with frost on your pillow.
> left: Write the dream down
  lore +small
  find lead_black_star_dream
  gain hollow_dreams
  say: Your notes fill four pages. In the morning you don't remember writing the last line: "It is not asleep. It is waiting."
> right: Ask Seraphine what it means
  meet seraphine
  rel seraphine +small
  find lead_black_star_dream
  gain hollow_dreams
  say: Seraphine listens, then hands you a sprig of lavender. "It won't stop the dreams," she says. "But it'll make them smell nicer."

@event hs_grey_stranger
title: A Man in Grey
arc: hollowstar
beat: 2
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
when: met(kael)
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A frozen fountain in a moonlit courtyard; a tall man in a grey coat facing a younger man, frost spreading from both.
text: Late at night in the courtyard, Kael is arguing with a tall man in a grey coat. The fountain between them has frozen mid-splash. "The door under the lake will be opened," the man says calmly. "By you, or by your sister. Your mother doesn't mind which."
> left: Try to slip away unseen
  guile +tiny
  mood -tiny
  find lead_man_in_grey
  say: You back into the shadows. The man in grey turns his head and looks straight at where you're hiding, then smiles and walks away. You don't sleep much.
> right: Step out and interrupt
  rel kael +large
  health -tiny
  find lead_man_in_grey
  flag confronted_grey
  say: "Everything all right?" The man in grey studies you, nods politely and leaves; the cold he leaves behind bites through your sleeves. Kael's hands are shaking. "You shouldn't have done that," he says. "...Thank you."

@event hs_founders_records
title: The Founders' Ledger
place: library
time: morning afternoon
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_founders_archive) and not clue(founders_ledger)
weight: 14
art: book
tags: mystery hollowstar study
chain: hollowstar
scene: A dusty archive vault, a giant ledger open on a lectern, one page carefully razored out.
text: In the archive vault you find the Founders' Ledger, three hundred years old. The entry for the academy's founding year has been cut out with a razor. But the page beneath still holds the impression of the pen.
> left: Leave it — this feels dangerous
  mood +tiny
  say: You close the ledger. The dust settles. Some doors are better left alone. Probably.
> right: Rub charcoal over the page
  challenge research apprentice+:
    win:
      flag knows_founders_seal
      find knows_founders_seal
      find founders_ledger
      lore +small
      say: Ghostly letters emerge: "Seven towers, seven locks. The Star sleeps beneath the water. The key is a star that holds no light." The founders built the academy as a seal.
    lose:
      lore +tiny
      say: The impression is too faint. You make out only three words: "...beneath the water..."

@event hs_restricted_founders
title: The Chained Drafts
place: restricted_section
time: midnight
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_founders_archive) and not clue(founders_ledger)
weight: 16
art: lock
tags: mystery hollowstar study
chain: hollowstar
scene: A dark aisle of the Restricted Section at midnight, a bundle of yellowed drafts chained to a shelf, the chain faintly glowing.
text: The archive's ledger has its founding page cut out. The Restricted Section keeps the founders' own drafts, chained to a shelf at the very back, and the chain is warm to the touch. Somewhere behind you, a book turns its own page.
> left: Work the chain loose
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      flag knows_founders_seal
      find founders_ledger
      find knows_founders_seal
      health -tiny
      say: The links give one by one, and burn your fingers doing it. The drafts say it plainly, in three hands: "Seven towers, seven locks. The Star sleeps beneath the water. The key is a star that holds no light." Lumenhold is a seal.
    lose:
      gain detention
      mood -small
      say: The chain shrieks like a ward. You're out of the window before the prefect arrives, but not before he sees your face. Detention, and a long look from the librarian.
> right: Copy the shelf-list instead
  lore +small
  mana -tiny
  find lead_seventh_tower
  say: The drafts' shelf-list is less guarded and nearly as strange. One entry reads only "Key: the seventh tower, top room. Do not lend." You copy it out by the light of a reading charm you have to keep alive for an hour, and it leaves you drained.

@event hs_boathouse_bell
title: The Hatch in the Boathouse
place: boathouse
time: evening night midnight
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_lake_breathed) and not clue(lake_bell)
weight: 16
art: bell
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: The inside of an old wooden boathouse at night, a square hatch open in the floorboards, stone steps leading down into dark water.
text: Under a coil of rotten rope in the boathouse there's a hatch, and under the hatch, stone steps going down into the lake. The air coming up smells of cold bronze. From somewhere below, very faint, a bell is tolling under the water.
> left: Go down the steps
  challenge feat apprentice:
    win:
      flag found_lake_tunnel
      find lake_bell
      health -tiny
      say: The steps become a tunnel under the lakebed, dry and ice-cold, running toward the sound. You follow it until you can see the bell's green rim in the dark ahead. Then you turn back, frozen to the bone, and remember every turning.
    lose:
      find lake_bell
      health -small
      say: The third step is ice. You go into the water to the chest and come up gasping, but you've seen it: a tunnel under the lake, running toward the bell. You walk home soaked.
> right: Listen at the waterline
  find lake_bell
  mood -small
  say: You lie on the boards with your ear to the gap. The bell tolls seven times, slow, and between the strokes you hear a draught moving under the lake, the way air moves in a corridor. Something down there is a door. You don't sleep well.

@event hs_seraphine_shadow
title: One Star Too Many
place: observatory
slot: evening
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: seraphine
when: clue(lead_black_star_dream) and met(seraphine) and not clue(second_shadow)
weight: 16
art: star
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: An observatory at night, the great telescope tilted down toward the window and the lake below, a seer pointing at the reflection of the stars in the water.
text: Seraphine has turned the great telescope down, not at the sky but at the lake, where the stars are reflected. "Look," she says. "In the water. There's one star too many, and it's dark." She counts under her breath. "It wasn't there in my dream. It was in yours."
> left: Chart it with her
  meet seraphine
  find second_shadow
  lore +small
  health -tiny
  say: You chart it till dawn on the cold floor: a small dark shape in the reflection that has no star above it, sitting exactly over the middle of the lake. Your knees never quite forgive you.
> right: Tell her about your dream
  meet seraphine
  find second_shadow
  rel seraphine +medium
  mood -small
  say: She finishes your sentences, three of them, before you've started them. Then she shows you the dark star in the water, right over the middle of the lake. You both stop talking for a long time.

@event hs_kael_truth
title: What Kael Is Running From
class: story
tone: eerie
when: (clue(lead_man_in_grey) or clues(hollowstar) >= 1) and rel(kael) >= 15 and not flag(kael_told)
actor: kael
weight: 16
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar social
chain: hollowstar
scene: Two students sitting on the edge of the frozen boathouse jetty at night, one with frost in his hair, both looking down at the black water.
text: Kael sits with you on the boathouse jetty. "My family serve something under this lake," he says at last. "They sent me here to open its door. I came to stop them. Some nights I'm not sure which I'll actually do."
> left: "Then we stop them together."
  flag kael_told kael_ally
  rel kael +large
  spark kael +tiny
  alignment +small
  find kael_family
  if bond(kael) == "none":
    bond kael friend
  say: He looks at you for a long moment, and the frost on the jetty melts a little. "Together," he repeats, as if trying out a word from another language.
> right: Tell the headmistress
  flag kael_told reported_kael
  rel kael -huge
  rel isolde +medium
  alignment +tiny
  find kael_family
  say: The headmistress thanks you gravely. The next day Kael is moved to a room in the headmistress's tower. He doesn't look at you anymore.

@event hs_star_mark
title: The Cold Coin Burns
class: story
tone: eerie
when: (flag(star_coin) or flag(bell_fragment)) and not has(star_mark) and not flag(threw_star)
weight: 12
art: star
tags: mystery hollowstar magic
chain: hollowstar
scene: A student's open palm, a pale star-shaped mark glowing on it, a blackened coin smoking on the floor beside them.
text: The black-starred relic you've been carrying burns suddenly, so cold it feels hot. When you drop it, there's a pale star-shaped mark on your palm. It hums when you're near the lake.
> left: Throw the relic into the lake
  flag threw_star
  unflag star_coin bell_fragment
  alignment +medium
  mood +tiny
  say: It sinks without a ripple. The mark on your hand fades — almost entirely. Something under the water sighs.
> right: Keep it. Feel the power.
  gain star_mark
  arcana +medium
  alignment -medium
  say: The mark pulses with every heartbeat. Spells come easier now. Much easier. That should probably worry you more than it does.

@event hs_grey_offer
title: An Offer in Grey
class: story
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 18 and (clues(hollowstar) >= 2 or alignment <= -30) and not flag(grey_offer_seen)
weight: 12
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: A grey-coated man sitting uninvited at a library table, a black velvet box open in front of him, the candles around him burning blue.
text: The man in grey is waiting at your library table. "You've been asking questions about the Star," he says pleasantly. "It's noticed you. It could make you extraordinary. All it wants is for someone to open a door."
> left: "Get out."
  alignment +small
  flag grey_offer_seen
  mood +tiny
  say: He inclines his head and leaves. The candles return to yellow. You realise your hands are trembling.
> right: "...What would it give me?"
  flag grey_offer_seen hollow_tempted
  arcana +medium
  alignment -medium
  say: He shows you, just for a moment. Power, endless and cold. When he's gone, you can still taste it.

@event hs_grey_invitation
time: evening night
title: A Seat at the Northern Table
class: story
tone: eerie
when: alignment <= -60 and turn >= 12 and not flag(hollow_courted)
weight: 16
art: letter
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: A black-edged letter on a dormitory pillow, its wax seal pressed with a star that has no light in it.
text: There is a letter on your pillow, sealed with a black star. The handwriting is beautiful. "The families have watched you with great interest," it says. "There is a seat for you at our table, when the door is opened. Come to the boathouse at midnight, or burn this. Either is an answer."
> left: Go to the boathouse
  flag hollow_courted hollow_tempted
  alignment -small
  guile +small
  health -small
  say: The man in grey is waiting with two cups of something hot. He talks to you as an equal for an hour. You come back with frost in your hair and the feeling of having been measured, and found to fit.
> right: Burn it
  alignment +medium
  mood -small
  say: The paper burns blue and slow, and smells of the lake. It takes a long time to go out. Climbing back from where you've been is slower still, but this is a step.

@event hs_grey_tests
title: The Good Argument
class: story
tone: eerie
when: alignment >= 30 and turn >= 14 and not flag(grey_tested)
weight: 12
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: A grey-coated man standing beside a student at the infirmary window, both looking down at a first-year with a bandaged arm.
text: The man in grey falls into step beside you outside the infirmary. "You help people," he says pleasantly. "I admire it. But think how many more you could help with real power. The Star doesn't care what it's used for. Only that someone uses it."
> left: "No."
  flag grey_tested
  alignment +small
  mood -tiny
  say: "No," you say. He smiles as if you'd said something charming, and leaves. The first-year in the window waves at you. You wave back, and your hand is shaking.
> right: "...How many more?"
  flag grey_tested hollow_tempted
  alignment -medium
  lore +small
  say: He tells you. The numbers are very large and very cold. That night, you dream of the lake from underneath, and you are not frightened in the dream.

@event hs_wardens_notice
title: The Headmistress Takes Note
class: story
tone: warm
actor: isolde
when: alignment >= 60 and turn >= 12 and not flag(wardens_noticed)
weight: 16
art: crown
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A tall woman in dark robes pausing on a stair to look down at one student among many, a silver ring glinting on her hand.
text: On the grand stair the headmistress stops beside you. "Several people have told me about you," she says, "and not one of them was complaining. That is rare." Her silver ring catches the light. "I keep a list of students I would trust with a door. Don't let it go to your head."
> left: "I'd be honoured."
  meet isolde
  flag wardens_noticed
  rel isolde +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: "Good," she says. "Honour is a heavy thing to carry. Practise." She walks on. You stand on the stair for some time.
> right: "What kind of door?"
  meet isolde
  flag wardens_noticed
  rel isolde +small
  lore +small
  say: Her short, delighted laugh. "The kind that ought to stay shut," she says. "Keep asking questions like that. Just not on the stairs."

@event hs_seventh_tower
title: The Seventh Tower
place: seventh_tower
slot: evening
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_seventh_tower) and not flag(star_key) and not flag(gave_star_key)
weight: 16
art: tower
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: The top of a narrow, abandoned tower, cobwebbed and moonlit, with a wall bearing a star-shaped recess.
text: The seventh tower has been locked for a century. You find a way in. At the very top, a single room: dust, moonlight, and a star-shaped hollow in the wall, holding something that does not reflect any light.
> left: Take it quietly
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      mood -small
      queue hs_key_breakfast in 1
      say: A key shaped like a star, black as a hole in the world. As you lift it, every candle in the academy goes out for one breath. You walk back in the dark with it cold against your ribs, and you don't sleep.
    lose:
      gain detention
      mood -small
      say: A ward shrieks. A prefect finds you on the stairs. You get detention and a very long look from the headmistress.
> right: Take it boldly
  challenge spell journeyman:
    win:
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      mana -small
      queue hs_key_breakfast in 1
      say: You tear through the ward with brute force, and it drains you to the bone. The key comes free. Every candle in the academy goes out for one breath, and somewhere below, a door hears it.
    lose:
      health -large
      say: The ward throws you down two flights of stairs.

@event hs_key_breakfast
title: Something of Mine
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: queued
defer: off_campus
actor: isolde
art: key
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: The high table at breakfast, the headmistress setting down her cup and looking along the hall at one student, the candles behind her newly lit.
text: At breakfast the headmistress sets down her cup and looks straight at you along the whole length of the hall. Afterwards she is waiting at the door. "Every candle in my academy went out," she says pleasantly, "and you have something of mine."
> left: Give her the key
  meet isolde
  unflag star_key
  flag gave_star_key wardens_noticed
  rel isolde +medium
  alignment +small
  say: She takes it in a gloved hand without looking at it. "Thank you. It will be where it is needed, on the night. So, I hope, will you." You feel lighter, and a little robbed.
> right: Keep it
  meet isolde
  flag kept_star_key
  rel isolde -medium
  say: A long pause. "Then keep it close," she says, "and never let it near the water before its time. People will come asking for it. Not all of them will ask." From then on, the man in grey always seems to know where you are.

@event hs_isolde_summons
title: The Headmistress Knows
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: final_year and month >= 3 and month <= 7 and (clues(hollowstar) >= 3 or flag(kael_ally) or flag(wardens_noticed) or flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts) or flag(sided_self))
priority: 45
actor: isolde
art: crown
tags: mystery hollowstar story
chain: hollowstar
scene: A circular study at the top of a tower, walls lined with sleeping portraits, the headmistress standing by a window that looks down on the lake.
text: The headmistress summons you to her tower. "You have been following the same thread I have," she says. "On the night of the Blossom moon, the seal will weaken. I need people I can trust beneath the lake. Or you can walk away. No one would blame you."
> left: Walk away
  meet isolde
  flag hollow_out
  mood +small
  say: "Wise," she says, and you can't tell if she means it. "Then stay above, and keep the first-years indoors."
> right: "I'll be there."
  alignment +small
  meet isolde
  flag warden_trial
  find star_key
  rel isolde +large
  arcana +small
  mood -small
  say: She presses a silver ward-ring into your hand. "{flag(star_key): The founders' key is with you. Keep it close.|{flag(gave_star_key): The founders' key is in my desk.|The founders' key is kept at the top of the seventh tower.}} On the night, it comes down with us. Learn quickly. You have until Blossomtide." You lose a little sleep over that every night.

@event hs_the_night
title: The Night the Lake Froze
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: final_year and month == 9 and (not flag(hollow_out) or flag(hollow_tempted) or flag(hollow_courted)) and (clues(hollowstar) >= 3 or flag(warden_trial) or flag(kael_ally) or flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts) or flag(sided_self) or flag(wardens_noticed) or flag(hollow_courted) or alignment <= -60)
priority: 70
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: The whole lake frozen white in the middle of spring, cracks glowing from beneath, students crowding the towers' windows.
text: In the middle of spring, the lake freezes in a single breath. Cracks glow beneath the ice. The bell under the water is tolling, and every candle in the academy leans toward the shore.
> left: Go down beneath the lake
  queue hs_tunnel now
  say: You run for the boathouse. Behind you, someone is shouting your name. You don't stop.
> right: Stay above and protect the students
  alignment +small
  health -large
  renown +large
  rel isolde +small
  flag hollow_held_line
  say: You hold the doors of the first-year tower all night against things made of frost and whispers. By dawn the lake thaws. Something below is still asleep — for now.

@event hs_tunnel
title: The Man in the Tunnel
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: queued
type: menu
priority: 95
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: A slick stone tunnel under the ice, lit blue from above, a tall man in a grey coat standing in the middle of it with his hands folded.
text: The tunnel from the boathouse runs down under the ice, slick and glowing blue. Halfway down, the man in grey is waiting{=flag(ilse_taken) and ", and Ilse stands beside him with her eyes on nothing" or ", alone, as if he has all night"}. "Go back up," he says pleasantly. "This isn't your door."
> fight: Break through him
  hint: Combat. Easier with Kael at your side.
  queue hs_threshold now
  if flag(kael_ally) or flag(winter_kael):
    challenge combat master-:
      win:
        flag hs_tunnel_clear
        health -small
        say: Kael's frost and your spell hit him together. He slides back along the ice, bows, and is simply not there any more. You go on with bruised ribs and a clear road.
      lose:
        health -large
        say: He swats the two of you aside like moths, then steps back to let you pass, smiling. "Go on, then." You go down bleeding, and late.
  else:
    challenge combat master- unlikely:
      win:
        flag hs_tunnel_clear
        health -small
        say: Your spell catches him square, and he slides back along the ice, surprised for the first time. He bows and is gone. You go on with bruised ribs and a clear road.
      lose:
        health -large
        say: He swats your spell aside, then steps back to let you pass, smiling. "Go on, then." You go down bleeding, and late.
> talk: Talk your way past
  hint: Charm. Easier if Ilse is safe, or you know what she was raised for.
  queue hs_threshold now
  if flag(ilse_saved) or flag(winter_ilse) or clue(ilse_truth):
    challenge negotiate master-:
      win:
        flag hs_tunnel_clear
        mood -small
        say: You tell him the Dumont children have chosen, both of them, and that you know exactly what they were raised for. For a moment he looks old. Then he steps aside. It costs you something to see that look.
      lose:
        mood -medium
        say: He listens courteously, agrees with every word, and lets you pass only once you've heard every word of his. You arrive shaken, and late.
  else:
    challenge negotiate master- unlikely:
      win:
        flag hs_tunnel_clear
        mood -small
        say: You talk fast and well, and somewhere in it he decides you're more trouble than you're worth. He steps aside with a little bow. Your hands don't stop shaking for a while.
      lose:
        mood -medium
        say: He listens courteously, agrees with every word, and lets you pass only once you've heard every word of his. You arrive shaken, and late.
> slip: Find another way down
  hint: Guile. Easier if you know the old tunnels.
  queue hs_threshold now
  if flag(found_lake_tunnel) or clue(lake_bell):
    challenge deceive master- likely:
      win:
        flag hs_tunnel_clear
        health -small
        say: You know a side passage he doesn't, the one the bell's rope once ran through. You come out below him, breathless and spent, and he never sees you go.
      lose:
        health -medium
        say: The side passage is half flooded. You come out soaked and freezing, below him, but late, and he calls a polite good evening after you.
  else:
    challenge deceive master- unlikely:
      win:
        flag hs_tunnel_clear
        mana -small
        say: You fold yourself into the dark and go round him along the wall, a breath at a time. It drains you, but he never turns his head.
      lose:
        health -medium
        say: He turns his head the moment you move. "Good evening." He lets you pass anyway, and the cold he leaves in your bones comes with you.

@event hs_threshold
title: The Founders' Words
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
type: menu
priority: 95
art: book
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: A wall of black stone at the end of a tunnel, carved with lines of script that drift when not looked at, a faint bell-tone hanging in the air.
text: The tunnel ends at a wall of black stone carved with the founders' words, in a script that drifts when you look away. Behind it the bell is tolling. The wall will open for someone who can read it, or someone who can make it.
> read: Read the founders' words
  hint: Lore. The founders' seal and the seven locks make it easier.
  queue hs_beneath now
  if clue(knows_founders_seal) and clue(seven_locks):
    challenge research master- likely:
      win:
        flag hs_threshold_read
        mood -tiny
        say: You've read these words before, in pieces, and you know where the locks fall. Said whole, they open the wall like a door, and the strain of it sits behind your eyes.
      lose:
        health -small
        mood -small
        say: You stumble on the last line, and the wall opens only a crack. You squeeze through it; it scrapes skin off your shoulder on the way.
  elif clue(knows_founders_seal) or clue(seven_locks) or flag(winter_isolde):
    challenge research master-:
      win:
        flag hs_threshold_read
        mood -tiny
        say: You know enough to guess the rest. The wall listens, and slides aside, and the strain of it sits behind your eyes.
      lose:
        health -small
        mood -small
        say: You stumble on the last line, and the wall opens only a crack. You squeeze through it; it scrapes skin off your shoulder on the way.
  else:
    challenge research master- unlikely:
      win:
        flag hs_threshold_read
        mood -tiny
        say: You don't know the words, but you know how words like these are built. Line by line, the wall gives way, and the strain of it sits behind your eyes.
      lose:
        health -small
        mood -small
        say: The script slides away from you. In the end the wall opens a crack on its own, as if amused. You squeeze through; it takes skin with it.
> force: Force the stone open
  hint: Arcana, and it hurts. Easier if Maud taught you her wards.
  queue hs_beneath now
  if flag(winter_maud):
    challenge spell master-:
      win:
        flag hs_threshold_read
        health -small
        say: You trace Maud's wards backwards into the stone, the way she showed you. The wall cracks down the middle and opens, and your hands ache to the elbow.
      lose:
        health -medium
        say: The stone fights back. You get through in the end, but your hands are raw and shaking.
  else:
    challenge spell master- unlikely:
      win:
        flag hs_threshold_read
        health -small
        say: You put everything you have into the stone, and it cracks down the middle. Your hands ache to the elbow.
      lose:
        health -medium
        say: The stone fights back. You get through in the end, but your hands are raw and shaking.

@event hs_beneath
title: The Door Beneath the Lake
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
type: menu
priority: 95
art: door
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: A vast domed cavern under the lake, a round door of black stone standing open a crack, and through it a star that is pure absence.
text: Beyond the wall, the round door. It stands open a crack. Through it, the Hollow Star looks at you — and it is beautiful, and it is hungry, and it knows your name.{=flag(kael_ally) and " Kael is beside you, wand raised, frost spreading from his feet." or ""}
> seal: Seal the door
  hint: Needs the star key, the founders' secret or a ward-ring. Arcana; preparation and the way down make it easier. It can fail.
  when: flag(star_key) or flag(knows_founders_seal) or flag(warden_trial) or flag(gave_star_key)
  alignment +small
  hs_prep = clue(seven_locks) + clue(star_key) + clue(ilse_truth) + (rel(kael) >= 18) + (rel(ilse) >= 18) + (rel(maud) >= 18) + (rel(isolde) >= 18) + 2 * (flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts)) + flag(sided_self) + (alignment >= 30) + (alignment >= 60) + (spell_level(starlight) >= 1) + (spell_level(ward) >= 1) + flag(wardens_noticed)
  hs_seal = hs_prep + 2 * flag(hs_tunnel_clear) + 2 * flag(hs_threshold_read)
  if hs_seal >= 13:
    challenge spell master sure:
      win:
        flag hollow_sealed
        renown +huge
        mood +large
        lose star_mark
        lose hollow_dreams
        queue hs_aftermath in 1
        say: {flag(knows_founders_seal): You speak the founders' words|You set the seal with everything you have}, and the door grinds shut. The Star screams without sound. Above, the ice cracks and the lake breathes again.
      lose:
        flag hollow_failed
        health -huge
        lose hollow_dreams
        queue hs_aftermath_lost in 1
        if flag(kael_ally) or flag(winter_kael):
          rel kael +large
          say: Your seal falters. Kael throws every ounce of frost in him into it, and it still isn't enough: the door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
        else:
          say: Your seal falters and breaks, and takes most of you with it. The door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
  elif hs_seal >= 9:
    challenge spell master likely:
      win:
        flag hollow_sealed
        renown +huge
        mood +large
        lose star_mark
        lose hollow_dreams
        queue hs_aftermath in 1
        say: {flag(knows_founders_seal): You speak the founders' words|You set the seal with everything you have}, and the door grinds shut. The Star screams without sound. Above, the ice cracks and the lake breathes again.
      lose:
